    {
      "_id": "1TzFWEnYeI8kXblP",
      "_key": "!journal.pages!rg50DlMYSzgbZeBv.1TzFWEnYeI8kXblP",
      "name": "Mortal Days",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>Nadia played bass in Capitol Hill bands for fifteen years. She was never famous, but she was the one who made everyone else sound good. In 2015, an infection damaged her left ear and took her off the stage. She moved to the mixing board, where she found what truly obsessed her: the human voice at three in the morning, when people tell the truth.</p>\n"
      },
      "sort": 200000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 2
      },
      "flags": {
        "seattle-by-night": {
          "origen": "pagina"
        }
      },
      "_stats": {
        "coreVersion": "14.365",
